    "summary": "Sculpture of a &#039;nat&#039;, deity, or lokapala. The figure is made of lacquered wood and  shown cross-legged on a fully gilded double-lotus throne, which is roughly triangular in shape. He wears a fine lower garment similar to a modern &#039;longyi&#039; (the Burmese sarong), decorated with yellow spirals on green, and red flowers on black; the material flows out between the knees ending in a gilded hem of curved pleats. His upper body is also clothed and on his chest and shoulders lies a fine golden cope. His hands are in clenched  fists.",
